    "methodology": "10,000-game solitaire heuristic. Sequencing: land drop, cheapest ramp, commander on affordability, combo/assembly pieces, biggest affordable threat, then other proactive spells. Mana is spent once per turn: the turn's pool is built after the land drop and each cast removes the sources it paid with, so the whole turn's casts (plus the combo and engine-activation gates, which are checked against what is left) never exceed the available mana (DEC-937). Sources that come online untapped mid-turn join the pool. Cast priority holds mana for the line instead of emptying the pool into filler (DEC-944). The commander, mana sources and the cards named by the deck's combo gate or KEY_COMBOS assembly slots are cast freely \u2014 mana sources are mana-positive across the turn and a piece cast advances a line rather than spending it. Every other cast is filler, and filler is skipped when the pool it would leave behind no longer pays for (a) a combo or assembly line that was reachable this turn before the cast, or (b) the deck's configured paid activations: one commander Egg activation while the hatch engine is online (DEC-938) and one Aggravated Assault combat while the enchantment is out with an attacker (DEC-940). The gate outranks the activations: an Egg activation, a Skullclamp equip or an extra combat is itself skipped when paying for it would lose a reachable gate. A hold the pool cannot afford at all is dropped rather than left blocking development. One activation of each kind is held, not an open-ended budget. Decks with no combo win condition, no KEY_COMBOS entry and no configured engine have no holds and sequence exactly as before. Meaningful board = pressure score >= 6 or 2+ threats. Lethal proxy = cumulative combat-pressure proxy >= 40; combat pressure uses mana-value-based creature scoring (min(8, MV) plus one for a listed combat keyword) so the curve stays comparable across the fleet \u2014 printed power/toughness is in the card metadata since DEC-940 but is deliberately not used for the damage sum, only for the combat modifiers' power gates. Combo lethal = at least one winConditions[] entry tagged kind:'combo' has all pieces present (hand, battlefield, or substitutable) and combined mana cost payable. Substitution priority for missing pieces: (1) bargain free-cast tutor (e.g. Beseech the Mirror) when a non-rock enchantment is on battlefield OR commander has been in play for 1+ turn (approximates Sauron-style amass token from real-game opponent casts); (2) type-matched regular tutor whose tutor_targets includes piece's card type and tutor_mv_cap permits piece's MV; (3) reanimation spell (decklist[].primary_role/secondary_role == 'recursion') for permanent pieces only \u2014 cost replaces piece's cast cost (treats piece as if in graveyard). Each substitute is consumed once per combo line. Tutors, non-permanent combo pieces, and reanimation spells are reserved from filler casting. v2 limitations: no literal graveyard tracking (reanim assumes piece could be in GY), no opponent interaction, no multi-turn assembly tracking, no stack-trigger ordering."
